lessons.concept:
A class is a blueprint. An object is one instance of that class. __init__ runs when an object is created; self refers to that object. A method is a function inside a class. Start with attributes and methods before inheritance.

Worked solution pattern:
class TestCase:
    def __init__(self, name, status):
        self.name = name
        self.status = status

    def result(self):
        return 'PASS' if self.status == 200 else 'FAIL'

test = TestCase('Login', 200)
print(test.result())

